	(lib_symbols)
	(text "RECEIVE CHANNEL (one sheet, instantiated as RX1 to RX4; keep all four identical for phase match)\nTO PLACE: patch antenna feed, ESD, band filter, MAX2659 LNA, MAX2682 mixer, IF amplifier, anti-alias filter.\nAUX_RF_IN / AUX_SEL: RF switch that swaps the patch for an external input and bypasses the band filter.\nUsed on RX1 only for the Starlink LNB (LNB_RF_IN, LNB_SEL). On RX2 to RX4 the pins are unconnected for now;\nplan is to fit the switch footprint on all four and mark the parts DNP on RX2 to RX4. Open for review.\nIF_OUT_P / IF_OUT_N assumes a differential IF driver into the MAX1193. Open for review.\nCONFIRMED PARTS (sourcing thread, 2026-11-19): MAX2659ELT+T, uDFN-6 1x1.5, JLCPCB C28043. MAX2682EUT+T, SOT-23-6, JLCPCB C242518.\nBand filter: Qorvo QPQ1065 footprint (1.4 x 1.2 mm) with a bypass link on all four channels, fitted on one (sourcing recommendation, Danilo can overrule).\nAux switch: PE4259-63, SC-70-6, JLCPCB C470892. LNB bias boost (RX1 use, 5 V to 13 V): MT3608, SOT-23-6, JLCPCB C84817.\nPLACEHOLDER: IF amplifier and 50 MHz band-pass anti-alias filter, not picked until the ADS gain budget is done.\nSIMULATION HAND-OFF: LNA match, mixer match, anti-alias filter, gain and noise budget."
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
